{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1561826-vulgar-magic-and-belief-in-the-technocracy-question","id":1561826,"title":"Vulgar Magic and Belief in the Technocracy Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-07-17T10:05:08-07:00","id":1561826,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Vulgar Magic and Belief in the Technocracy Question","content":"Hey guys, first time poster but I've been asking this question everywhere-<br /> <br /> Im just getting into Mage and the technocracy is really interesting, especially something like the syndicate but I'm a bit hung up.<br /> <br /> I know that the highest echelons of the Union KNOW that reality warping &quot;magic&quot; is real, they just define it as a natural part of their world. I KNOW that technocrats are much more tied into their foci and essentially try to or would not even consider casting vulgar magics as they don't believe that's even possible.<br /> <br /> My question is this: You're a technocrat, a syndicate member. You buy and sell for a living. You literally can somehow, will money to always be in your safe the next morning with a few phone calls to people you vaguely know or have never even seen. You know quintessence exists, but you call it market value and potential earnings. You somehow always have an intuition on the best places to gain this market value. This is all of course, coincidental, small rituals that you might not even know why you do it, but you do. A few phone calls and the right words and suddenly all your business deals workout just fine, it's all very boring really, that's just how the economy works! <br /> <br /> But say one day you get jumped by one of those reality deviants in an ally. They use their sick, interdimensional abilities to conjure fire from some different dimension and hurl it at you. What do you, a simple enlightened business man do? You're a red blooded American but you forgot your gun at home. Your security detail is out for lunch....would a good syndicate technocrat hide behind a dumpster, pull out a calculator and with a few button presses cast &quot;Liquidate asset-Person&quot; and literally watch as the reality freak in front of them disintegrates into economic value like coins and dollars? Or would the syndicate members run and make some &quot;calls&quot; to get a speedy driver there in a flash or have a &quot;totally real and not golemn/metaphysical&quot; security team with M4's show up within a minutes time? <br /> <br /> What exactly tells a technocrat that he is &quot;awakened&quot;? what does &quot;Enlightened&quot; mean to them?<br /> <br /> For the syndicate- Do they look at the seemingly magical or unexplainable things they do every day with making money just appear, sensing the value or &quot;mana&quot; in others or places, putting &quot;effort&quot; I.E. Quintessence into things to get value out of it, and simply see this as a natural, if not quiet &quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;magical&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot; extension of what the &quot;economy&quot; and hyper-economics is capable of? Do they really look at the economy almost as such a complex thing that it can make impossible things happen because they are JUST that good at it? <br /> <br /> Then what if they snap, what if they in a moment of panic DO liquidate someone with absolutely no explainable way of showing how? Raw panic let them cast a vulgar &quot;spell&quot; and suck the &quot;value&quot; out of a mage and turn him into 145 dollar and 39 cents in the Unionists hand? Do they snap and go crazy? Do they schizophrenically explain it away as a homeless man that shoved stolen money at them? <br /> <br /> I love the setting but I just want to know the exact mindset of these guys in the day to day. I know the highest levels know all about the war, &quot;Mages&quot;, the consensus and what it means, and their own &quot;abilities&quot; but, I'd just like a few examples like my own above to help me understand better.<br /> <br /> - Side note: I know they reason away &quot;:avatars&quot; for themselves as inspiration or their genius intellect given form, but how does that square away with the progenitors having a pseduo-metaphysical operation to surgically REMOVE the avatars of awakened/format sleepers? They're just lobotomizing people? Why would they do that when those people could be [part of their ascended world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29128-internetflexing","name":"Internetflexing","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T10:29:53-07:00","id":1561827,"title":"","content":"Simplest way to explain it is:<br /> <br /> Technocrats are perfectly aware they make Magic. They just find calling it &quot;magic&quot; a sign of simple-mindness.<br /> <br /> Also, they definitely make Vulgar effects, don't worry. Their effects are as susceptible to Paradox as anyone else's. They just have an easier time being coincidental. By the way, a Vulgar effect isn't a reality-breaking scenario in their head, it's just a minor offense if done without good reason, and even that's just because Paradox endangers the mission.<br /> <br /> Mages are hyper-philosophers. They don't &quot;know they're Awakened/Enlightened&quot; in the sense of knowing they're a supernatural splat. They have theories about reality, and from their POV they're completely right: it's impossible to prove a Mage is wrong about virtually whatever they believe. This is exactly the same for all factions.<br /> <br /> From experience all they can say for sure is that they're that good. And then, that there are other people so good that they can also explore rules of reality normal people are just too dumb to realize, even if those other people have ludicrous theories that seem to work, but surely not because their bizarre theories are right.<br /> <br /> Everything else is just the result of having the Awakened interacting for thousands of years. What you see in the books isn't strictly reality: it is the standard theory of the Traditions. And it has failure points, mind you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T10:38:01-07:00","id":1561828,"title":"","content":"On Instruments: the Traditions have several theories for how Will alone changes the world. For some you're pleading to a god, for others the world is an illusion you can alter through contact with the Collective Unconscious. The Order of Hermes says it is because Will shapes reality, and their early influence made that the Council's party line.<br /> <br /> Technocrats also have theories for that and don't bat and eye to this, but they believe their method precludes such crude and dangerous practice, that would require a training they don't have, anyway.<br /> <br /> A Mage's reality bending effect is so powerful that it self-inflicts limitations. Current Mages have Spheres because they believe they have Spheres. Technocrats can't use Magic without Instruments because they believe they can't. And no amount of despair will change that, as their belief is reality and their Will is to strong to change for any reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}